Hi all — attaching a quick retry wrapper example and confirming the sample repo will be up by COB Oct 12. Connector sample includes a small harness to simulate 50–150 RPS and an injected failure mode.

Retry wrapper (Node, simplified):
async function withRetries(fn, opts = {}) {
  const maxAttempts = opts.attempts || 5;
  const base = opts.base || 200; // ms
  for (let i = 1; i <= maxAttempts; i++) {
    try {
      return await fn();
    } catch (err) {
      const shouldRetry = err.code >= 500 || err.code === 'ECONNRESET' || err.code === 429;
      if (!shouldRetry || i === maxAttempts) throw err;
      const jitter = Math.random() * 100;
      const backoff = Math.min(base * Math.pow(2, i - 1) + jitter, 8000);
      await new Promise(r => setTimeout(r, backoff));
    }
  }
}

Instrumentation: each retry increments a metric: redwood.connector.retry.count with labels {client_id, endpoint, attempt}. We'll surface these to Datadog and include alert rules: > 50 retries/min sustained triggers an ops pager.

